meta {
  name: end-to-end-order-flow
}

docs {
  Creates a unique test product, places an order for it through APISIX,
  waits for async delivery, then verifies kitchen-service received it twice
  (once via the kitchen_queue, once via the orders pubsub exchange - see
  kitchen-service/server.ts) and that inventory-service's stock dropped by
  the order quantity twice - once per delivery.

  Each decrement is kitchen-service calling inventory-service through its
  Envoy sidecar (INVENTORY_SERVICE_URL -> 127.0.0.1:20032), i.e. through the
  Consul Connect mesh - this flow is what that plumbing is actually for.

  Run the four requests in order (Bruno's Runner respects their seq).
}
